lines+=['A runtime NFT destination check can prevent prohibited transfer while leaving the original immutable claim stranded; it is containment, not recovery. Arbitrary rescue, mutable recipients or a changed payout schedule require an explicit design choice. CREATE2/prevrandao address changes alone are not a complete fix. A delivery fallback must retain all funds it promises to pay and cannot trust a malicious token to honestly certify delivery.','', 'Donation custody remains separate from liabilities: unsolicited ERC20/NFT/ETH may be intentionally unrescuable, while tracked claims can still be exact. Recipient blacklisting, quote freeze/upgrade and unsupported fee/rebase behavior remain conditional dependency/configuration risks. Existing scope and severity disagreements are retained; none was resolved by inferring owner acceptance.','', '## Artifacts and checks','',f"Updated register: [findings-register-final-draft.json]({O/'findings-register-final-draft.json'}). It contains {len(d['findings'])} findings/observations, {len(d['assurance_issues'])} assurance issues and {d['counts']['original_attributions_preserved_and_added']} attribution records. Counts include accepted, rejected, informational and advisory items; they are not a vulnerability count.",'', 'The companion ADDENDUM-SEAL.json records hashes for this supplement, the updated register, the reproducible generation script and the unchanged original files. No original seal is overwritten.']
(O/'RECONCILIATION-ADDENDUM.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
